{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791564618,"nonce":"1cDQ/xZO5Lu+Hm4pc+DI+k5aiCg=","title":"Constant-time insert and remove on the native layout tree","message":"LayoutContext::insert_before, detach and remove_child (blinc_abi 88b8c7f) make one native edit each, but only append is constant time. Inserting before a sibling, moving, or detaching rebuilds the parent's taffy child list through LayoutTree::children and replace_children, which is linear in the number of siblings and allocates a Vec.\n\nBlinc's LayoutTree keeps its TaffyTree private and exposes only add_child and replace_children. A true constant-time edit (apart from taffy's own Vec shift) needs LayoutTree to expose taffy's insert_child_at_index and remove_child, which is an upstream Blinc change.\n\n**Measure first**\nKeyed list reorders on a few thousand children, with the large-tree benchmark from d1a4fbe.","files":null}]}